# Version control (migrated rule)

Canonical SemVer policy for this repo:

- Keep one numeric SemVer across:
  - `version-control/version`
  - `package.json` version
  - `version-control/changelog.md`
- Milestone-derived mapping follows `version-control/governance/commands/milestones.md`.
- Do not skip milestone versions.
- `verify:version` must pass before gate promotion.
- Gate pass does **not** equal milestone closure; milestone status is recorded separately in `version-control/governance/commands/implementation-status.md`.

## SemVer source of truth

- Use numeric SemVer only (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, no `v`) in files.
- Canonical version file: `version-control/version`.
- `README.md`, `package.json`, and release notes must align with `version-control/version`.

## Auto bump workflow

- Hook trigger config: `.cursor/hooks.json` (`afterFileEdit`)
- Hook implementation: `version-control/hooks/after-file-edit-version-sync.mjs`
- Script entry: `npm run version:auto` (`version-control/scripts/auto-version-bump.mjs`)
- Baseline source: highest **Closed** milestone in `version-control/governance/commands/implementation-status.md`
- Per-change bump: PATCH bump once per HEAD batch

## Changelog & context workflow

- `version-control/changelog.md`:
  - Follow the latest entry format exactly (same heading shape and bullet style as the previous write).
  - Under `Unreleased`, each write uses one title line:
    - `### [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS LOCAL] [x.y.z] <one-sentence summary>`
  - The `x.y.z` value must equal `version-control/version` at write time.
  - Keep detail bullets directly under that title (no extra nested section required).
  - Record only changes that will be pushed to GitHub.
  - Changes limited to ignored/local-only paths (e.g. `.cursor/**`, `version-control/context-control.md`, local hook/state files) do **not** need changelog entries.
- `version-control/context-control.md`:
  - Append-only work log.
  - Timestamp uses local machine time in heading format: `### [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS LOCAL]`.
  - Keep one blank line between entries.

## Milestone policy summary

- Milestone mapping: `M0 -> 0.1.0` ... `M10 -> 1.0.0` (see `version-control/governance/commands/milestones.md`).
- Do not skip milestone-derived versions.
- `verify:version` and stage gate checks must pass before milestone closure.
- Keep closure records aligned in `version-control/governance/commands/implementation-status.md`.
